1.Verify Java version : java -version
2.If java is not available : sudo apt install fontconfig openjdk-21-jre -y
3.Install Jenkins : sudo apt install jenkins -y
4. Start jenkins : sudo systemctl start jenkins
5. Enable Jenkins at boot : sudo systemctl enable jenkins
6.Check Jenkins status: sudo systemctl status jenkins
7.Access Jenkins DashBoard: http://localhost:8080
8.Get Jenkins password : sudo cat /var/lib/jenkins/secrets/initialAdminPassword
Paste it in Jenkins Administrator password box
9.Install plugins
Customize Jenkins
Select: Install suggested plugins
Wait until the installation finishes.
10.Create Jenkins user: Enter username, password, email, Full name(Save and continue)
11.Jenkins URL : It shows http://localhost:8080
Keep it as it is and save and continue

